sekai-kb template marker.

While this file exists, the genericity + English-only gates run in TEMPLATE MODE:
they scan the WHOLE repository, not just the code trees. The sekai-kb template
ships zero real-place strings, so the whole tree — including knowledge/,
place.config.ts, and docs/ — must stay free of denylisted place names and CJK
codepoints.

`npm run init` (the adoption wizard) deletes this file when you adopt the template.
The gates then revert to INSTANCE MODE, where knowledge/ and place.config.ts
legitimately carry your place's identity. Each gate states its own instance root
set: check-genericity.sh scans src/, scripts/, tests/, workers/,
.agents/skills/; check-english-only.mjs scans src/, scripts/, tests/, workers/,
.agents/skills/; the two lists agree today but are never merged into one claim, so
either gate can gain a root without the other. See both scripts under scripts/ci/.
